@startuml
hide empty description
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam NoteFontSize 12
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam ranksep 70
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #C8E6C9
  BorderColor #7A7A7A
  ArrowColor #555555
}
title PolyNTU dialog map: bracket history and creator resolution on the Market page (UC-14)

state "Bracket history\ncollapsed" as Collapsed
state "Closed tab" as ClosedTab
state "Voided tab" as VoidedTab
state "Resolved tab" as ResolvedTab
state "Derive signing key" as Derive
state "Resolve control" as Control
state "Awaiting the authority\n(read-only notice)" as Waiting

Collapsed : tab bar with counts:\nClosed (n), Voided (n), Resolved (n)
ClosedTab : brackets awaiting resolution
VoidedTab : voided brackets, "View" opens one
ResolvedTab : resolved brackets and results,\n"View" opens one
Derive : account password field,\n"Derive signing key"
Control : outcome selector and "Resolve"\nper closed bracket
Waiting : "The automatic resolver is answering"\nor "Awaiting the resolution authority"

[*] --> Collapsed : the series has closed,\nvoided or resolved brackets

Collapsed --> ClosedTab : open the Closed tab
Collapsed --> VoidedTab : open the Voided tab
Collapsed --> ResolvedTab : open the Resolved tab
ClosedTab --> Collapsed : click the open tab again
VoidedTab --> Collapsed : click the open tab again
ResolvedTab --> Collapsed : click the open tab again

state closedChoice <<choice>>
ClosedTab --> closedChoice
closedChoice --> Waiting : [not the creator,\nor authority is not the creator]
closedChoice --> Control : [creator and the cached key\nmatches the published key]
closedChoice --> Derive : [creator but no matching key\nin this browser]

Derive --> Control : password derives the\npublished public key
Derive --> Derive : wrong password\n(error banner)
Control --> ClosedTab : "Resolve" signs and submits;\nthe bracket moves to Resolved
Control --> Control : submission rejected\n(error banner)

note bottom of Derive
  The signing key is derived from the account
  password (ADR 0007) and cached in this browser at
  sign-in, surviving reloads. This state appears
  when the cache is empty or holds another account's
  key: a browser that never signed in with the
  password, or one where the series was published
  elsewhere.
end note
@enduml
